                      VIDEO  -- NORMAL AND REVERSE


As we supply the Apple Lisa Unix System V, the screen background is black
and the characters are white. You can change this easily, since we have
provided you with 2 command scripts, vidnor (for black background) and
vidrev (for white background).

There are a few peculiarities of which you must be aware:

1	Running vidnor and vidrev WILL change the screen. However,
	it is also necessary to "inform" Unix that you have made the change.
	This is done by entering:
		TERM=newterm   (where newterm is either vtl or vtlrev)
		export TERM
	from the keyboard. Unfortunately, these TERM commands do not
	have any effect when issued from within a script.

b	vidnor and vidrev do not work properly when you are running
	under the cshell (csh).

Here is an example of going from normal to reverse video.

vidrev
TERM=vtlrev
export TERM
 .
 .
 .

To go back to normal video

vidnor
TERM=vtl
export TERM
 .
 .
 .

